-- A user-defined infix operator is admitted as a later operand of a
-- built-in operator (AND, OR, comparisons, arithmetic), exactly as it is
-- already admitted as the first operand, inside parentheses, and as a
-- prefix call.
-- It binds tighter than every built-in operator, as prefix application
-- does, so the bare spelling and the parenthesised spelling mean the same.

§ `The operator`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
a `exceeds by at least` b MEANS a AT LEAST b

§ `After AND and OR`

-- The bare spelling: the operator is the second operand of AND.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ok plain` n x IF
    TRUE AND n `exceeds by at least` x

-- The same, parenthesised (always admitted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ok parenthesised` n x IF
    TRUE AND (n `exceeds by at least` x)

-- The same, as a prefix call (always admitted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ok prefix` n x IF
    TRUE AND `exceeds by at least` n x

-- The operator as the first operand (always admitted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ok first` n x IF
    n `exceeds by at least` x AND TRUE

-- The operator on both sides of the connective.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ok both sides` n x IF
    n `exceeds by at least` x AND x `exceeds by at least` 0

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bare and` p n x IF p AND n `exceeds by at least` x

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `parenthesised and` p n x IF p AND (n `exceeds by at least` x)

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bare or` p n x IF p OR n `exceeds by at least` x

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `parenthesised or` p n x IF p OR (n `exceeds by at least` x)

#EVAL `ok plain` 5 3
#EVAL `ok plain` 1 3
#EVAL `ok parenthesised` 5 3
#EVAL `ok prefix` 5 3
#EVAL `ok first` 5 3
#EVAL `ok both sides` 5 3
#EVAL `ok both sides` 5 8

-- Bare and parenthesised agree on every combination of a Boolean and a
-- comparison that holds or fails.
#ASSERT `bare and` TRUE 5 3 EQUALS `parenthesised and` TRUE 5 3
#ASSERT `bare and` TRUE 1 3 EQUALS `parenthesised and` TRUE 1 3
#ASSERT `bare and` FALSE 5 3 EQUALS `parenthesised and` FALSE 5 3
#ASSERT `bare and` FALSE 1 3 EQUALS `parenthesised and` FALSE 1 3
#ASSERT `bare or` TRUE 5 3 EQUALS `parenthesised or` TRUE 5 3
#ASSERT `bare or` TRUE 1 3 EQUALS `parenthesised or` TRUE 1 3
#ASSERT `bare or` FALSE 5 3 EQUALS `parenthesised or` FALSE 5 3
#ASSERT `bare or` FALSE 1 3 EQUALS `parenthesised or` FALSE 1 3

-- Known answers for the bare spelling.
#ASSERT `bare and` TRUE 5 3
#ASSERT NOT `bare and` TRUE 1 3
#ASSERT NOT `bare and` FALSE 5 3

§ `Inside a CONSIDER arm`

-- The bare spelling after AND, in the body of a WHEN arm.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arm plain` m n IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE AND n `exceeds by at least` x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- The operator alone in the arm (always admitted).
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arm alone` m n IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST x THEN n `exceeds by at least` x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- The operator parenthesised after AND in the arm (always admitted).
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arm parenthesised` m n IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE AND (n `exceeds by at least` x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

#EVAL `arm plain` (JUST 3) 5
#EVAL `arm plain` (JUST 8) 5
#EVAL `arm plain` NOTHING 5
#EVAL `arm alone` (JUST 3) 5
#EVAL `arm parenthesised` (JUST 3) 5

#ASSERT `arm plain` (JUST 3) 5 EQUALS `arm parenthesised` (JUST 3) 5
#ASSERT `arm plain` (JUST 8) 5 EQUALS `arm parenthesised` (JUST 8) 5
#ASSERT `arm plain` NOTHING 5 EQUALS `arm parenthesised` NOTHING 5

§ `After a comparison and an arithmetic operator`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
x SCALEDBY y MEANS x TIMES y

-- A bare-word operator is admitted the same way.
-- It binds tighter than PLUS on either side, so both spell 16.
#EVAL 10 PLUS 2 SCALEDBY 3
#EVAL 2 SCALEDBY 3 PLUS 10
#ASSERT 10 PLUS 2 SCALEDBY 3 EQUALS 2 SCALEDBY 3 PLUS 10

-- The operator as the later operand of a comparison.
#EVAL TRUE EQUALS 5 `exceeds by at least` 3
#EVAL FALSE EQUALS 5 `exceeds by at least` 3
#EVAL 2 SCALEDBY 3 EQUALS 6 AND TRUE

§ `An operand that is not known`

ASSUME `unknown count` IS A NUMBER

-- When the first operand settles the connective, the unknown operand is
-- never needed, and the bare and parenthesised spellings agree.
#EVAL FALSE AND `unknown count` `exceeds by at least` 3
#EVAL FALSE AND (`unknown count` `exceeds by at least` 3)
#EVAL TRUE OR `unknown count` `exceeds by at least` 3
#EVAL TRUE OR (`unknown count` `exceeds by at least` 3)

§ `A multi-keyword operator`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      lo IS A NUMBER
      hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
x `lies from` lo `up to` hi MEANS x AT LEAST lo AND x AT MOST hi

#EVAL TRUE AND 5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9
#EVAL TRUE AND 12 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9
#EVAL FALSE OR 5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9

§ `Written as a MEANS or IS definition`

-- The ordinary way to write a rule is a definition with a MEANS or IS body,
-- not a DECIDE ... IF condition or a directive.
-- Each body below puts the operator after a built-in operator.

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`bare in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND 5 `exceeds by at least` 3

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`parenthesised in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND (5 `exceeds by at least` 3)

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arithmetic in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND 6 SCALEDBY 2 EQUALS 12

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`parenthesised arithmetic in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND (6 SCALEDBY 2) EQUALS 12

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`multi-keyword in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND 5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`parenthesised multi-keyword in a MEANS body` MEANS TRUE AND (5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9)

-- An IS body whose expression starts on the next line.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `multi-keyword in an IS body` IS
    TRUE AND 5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `parenthesised multi-keyword in an IS body` IS
    TRUE AND (5 `lies from` 1 `up to` 9)

#ASSERT `bare in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `arithmetic in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `multi-keyword in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `multi-keyword in an IS body`
#ASSERT `bare in a MEANS body` EQUALS `parenthesised in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `arithmetic in a MEANS body` EQUALS `parenthesised arithmetic in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `multi-keyword in a MEANS body` EQUALS `parenthesised multi-keyword in a MEANS body`
#ASSERT `multi-keyword in an IS body` EQUALS `parenthesised multi-keyword in an IS body`

§ `A call spread over several lines`

-- A chain split across lines needs parentheses, with a new line after the
-- opening one.
-- Without them every keyword must be on the operand's own line, as below.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `spread over lines` n x IF
    TRUE AND (
        n
        `exceeds by at least`
        x
    )

#EVAL `spread over lines` 5 3
#EVAL `spread over lines` 1 3
